//fldigi macro definition file extended
// This file defines the macro structure(s) for the digital modem program, fldigi
// It also serves as a basis for any macros that are written by the user
//
// The top line of this file should always be the first line in every macro 
// definition file (.mdf) for the fldigi program to recognize it as such.
//

//
// Macro # 1
/$ 0 CQ@#-2+
<TX>\n
CQ CQ CQ de <MYCALL> <MYCALL>\n
CQ CQ CQ de <MYCALL> <MYCALL> pse k  \n
<RX><AFTER:60>

//
// Macro # 2
/$ 1 ANS @>|
<TX><CALL> <CALL> de <MYCALL> <MYCALL> kn\n
<RX>

//
// Macro # 3
/$ 2 QSO @>>
<TX><CALL> de <MYCALL>\n


//
// Macro # 4
/$ 3 KN @||
btu <CALL> de <MYCALL> kn\n
<RX>


//
// Macro # 5
/$ 4 SK @||
 <CALL> de <MYCALL> sk\n
<RX>

//
// Macro # 6
/$ 5 Me/Qth
Name here is <MYNAME> in <MYQTH>, <MYST> at <MYLOC>. \n


//
// Macro # 7
/$ 6 Brag
\n
Rig: IC-7300\n
Pwr: <TX_PWR>W\n
Ant: <ANTENNA>\n
Cmp: M4 MacMini\n
Sw : <VER>\n


//
// Macro # 8
/$ 7 AGN? @>|
<TX>AGN? AGN?\n
<RX>

//
// Macro # 9
/$ 8 T/R
<TX/RX>

//
// Macro # 10
/$ 9 Tx @>>
<TX>

//
// Macro # 11
/$ 10 Rx @||
<RX>

//
// Macro # 12
/$ 11 TX @>|
<TX> <CALL> de <MYCALL> k\n
<RX>

//
// Macro # 13
/$ 12 Signal Good
I have a good copy: <INFO1>\n


//
// Macro # 14
/$ 13 Rough Copy
I have an ok copy, loosing some characters: <INFO1>\n


//
// Macro # 15
/$ 14 WX 
<EXEC>fltools wx</EXEC>\n


